{
  "_comment": "⛔ QUARANTINED scene styles (five-line split, Aaron 2026-08-12): this dormant bench's style blocks, vendored OUT of ui_theme.json (a scene's values belong in its scene file). They move into this bench's own .scene.json at its migration — do not grow this file. Colors are $token refs into ui_theme.json's theme.tokens; a `theme` key here is refused as a palette fork.",
  "pocclusters": {
    "_comment": "flicker-pocclusters 'Cluster Editor' HUD — TWO declarative panels walked by flicker-widgets run_ui, built to the design mock (DesignSync project a39150df, 'Cluster Editor HUD.dc.html'). LEFT 'main' panel = header + mode pill, a Readout box (title + Cam/Grid/Move/Diag rows + Pick + a walk-only row + Esc hint), the 6 Debug-Overlay toggles in a 2-column grid, and a Move-speed slider. RIGHT 'inspector' panel = shown only when a face is picked: header + subtitle + a 7-column table (Corner / X Y Z local / wX wY wZ world) over the selected voxel's 8 corners. Stat + cell strings are pre-formatted in Rust (hud_model) and bound by name via text_bind; toggles + slider are two-way binds. Every colour is a $token (single palette source = this file's theme.tokens). Caps labels now carry the mock's letter-spacing (the `label` font role tracks them); numeric cells set `tracking = 0` on their text nodes so the fixed-width columns stay aligned. Corner runes ARE rendered (the `Prism Rune` face + `runes` config: each panel is a `stack` overlaying 4 Elder Futhark glyphs — top two rune-light over a feathered `rune_halo` panel, bottom two bronze). Panel headers carry a bronze ✦/◈ icon with lead/trail spacers that clear the corner runes; the Esc hint sits in a bordered `keycap`; the inspector closes with a colour-coded ◆ local / wX·wY·wZ world legend. Remaining mock flourishes a vector HUD still can't do (gem glyphs, runePulse animation, inset shadows) are omitted. The separate `hud`/`voxel` sections still serve the legacy voxel-cluster example — keep them distinct.",
